  "biography": {
    "plain_text": "Hans-Günther Schmid was a German entrepreneur whose alloy-wheel businesses financed his involvement in Formula One. He helped build ATS before exchanging his stake for Rial and its factory at Fußgönheim. His son Ralf and nephew Michael later took over management, continuing the family's involvement in wheel manufacturing after his withdrawal.",
    "confidence": {
